      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name} i've noticed that the SDK itself also adds onto the avatar size. If a avatar is like 9.9MB the sdk will add onto it and make it go to 10 or higher.\n\nIf they just gave more headroom to work with we could get nice avatars with lots of features on quest.\n\nBut they dont seem to really listen since there's also a canny post regarding very poor for mobile. Which people suggested to remove with putting a warning in place before enabling them as an example..",
